{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"We use 3 separate tools to help manage our dependencies and prevent us from unnecessarily bloating the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules"},{"type":"text","value":" directory."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sherif","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sherif"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sherif ensures that all references to a dependency throughout the monorepo are on the same version"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This helps avoid pnpm resolution issues, such as type conflicts from having 2+ incompatible versions of the same dependency installed"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"knip","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Knip"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Knip is able to detect unused dependencies within "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package.json"},{"type":"text","value":" files"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This leads to fewer packages getting installed unnecessarily by developers"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"renovate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renovate"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renovate is a bot which runs on GitHub to scan for outdated or insecure dependencies"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This reduces the burden on maintainers by automatically submitting PRs"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"sherif","text":"Sherif","level":3},{"id":"knip","text":"Knip","level":3},{"id":"renovate","text":"Renovate","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nWe use 3 separate tools to help manage our dependencies and prevent us from unnecessarily bloating the `node_modules` directory.\n\n### Sherif\n\n- Sherif ensures that all references to a dependency throughout the monorepo are on the same version\n- This helps avoid pnpm resolution issues, such as type conflicts from having 2+ incompatible versions of the same dependency installed\n\n### Knip\n\n- Knip is able to detect unused dependencies within `package.json` files\n- This leads to fewer packages getting installed unnecessarily by developers\n\n### Renovate\n\n- Renovate is a bot which runs on GitHub to scan for outdated or insecure dependencies\n- This reduces the burden on maintainers by automatically submitting PRs\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: dependencies\ntitle: Dependencies\n---\n\nWe use 3 separate tools to help manage our dependencies and prevent us from unnecessarily bloating the `node_modules` directory.\n\n### Sherif\n\n- Sherif ensures that all references to a dependency throughout the monorepo are on the same version\n- This helps avoid pnpm resolution issues, such as type conflicts from having 2+ incompatible versions of the same dependency installed\n\n### Knip\n\n- Knip is able to detect unused dependencies within `package.json` files\n- This leads to fewer packages getting installed unnecessarily by developers\n\n### Renovate\n\n- Renovate is a bot which runs on GitHub to scan for outdated or insecure dependencies\n- This reduces the burden on maintainers by automatically submitting PRs\n"}
